  "claimVersions": [
    {
      "id": "claim-version:80a7d871-70ea-456f-951d-911fae089b49",
      "claimId": "claim:04356a4b-e852-424a-a8dd-67499e8916f2",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-72e69bbe56e3cb18dee9e33c805ba5492f91074f0d713b7cae5a22b421791349"
      },
      "text": "(1−ε) d_TV(P,Q) ≤ D̃ ≤ (1+ε) d_TV(P,Q) with probability at least 1−η.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-548b6146e3351a8d1a708e5a8aa8efdc4b0fa3717821858ed1ab07d6515257f1",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-72e69bbe56e3cb18dee9e33c805ba5492f91074f0d713b7cae5a22b421791349"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:5eacfce2-8aa2-41b8-b234-0670f00f5120",
      "claimId": "claim:bd4e1ae5-c93b-4c58-8888-183e530123ac",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-f61b01b67928c332e3d2f33e9e4546ae5659c56542d97772e3df3e510750ff57"
      },
      "text": "Conditionally on all L sparsifications succeeding, the root coreset reproduces the exact root functional to within (1±δ)^L, and more generally the invariant holds at every constructed region with exponent ℓ(S), for all queries a simultaneously.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-6c40217727aba83b5cf4f2aba1a45d5497284c97809c4ca8a711fdcc8601f20f",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-f61b01b67928c332e3d2f33e9e4546ae5659c56542d97772e3df3e510750ff57"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:8cb3a593-b55f-46c2-a778-36b925c4f5a5",
      "claimId": "claim:1f25ea2f-62e2-49de-8923-089f1922ac76",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-f878b85ac1a1cd76056d8d7353793ca4283bbfc0ed9150e7b1a43669d4f1a745"
      },
      "text": "Sum gates/layers introduce no error and no domain expansion (a fixed linear reparametrisation of features preserves every linear test).",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-4cf45c603136787166ac3fed28b74ad69b973da9d390e32dbfe192bd717adc11",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-f878b85ac1a1cd76056d8d7353793ca4283bbfc0ed9150e7b1a43669d4f1a745"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:b9c0acfb-51b4-4c13-bea9-93eca0db1a08",
      "claimId": "claim:808a7dcf-0b1c-48f7-97b1-5ae20389fc0a",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-ab071a0749cff8df9e01f2de4351e9ca5666bb87e784e4222136df8044c9b266"
      },
      "text": "The exact root sum ∑_x |⟨a_TV, Φ_root(x)⟩| equals 2 d_TV(P,Q), and the root coreset sum equals 2D̃.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-24690d92875aafcd6454bdda82f34e48f06b5a69272b6889e719a0d2c4be9c87",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-ab071a0749cff8df9e01f2de4351e9ca5666bb87e784e4222136df8044c9b266"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:6f33b194-e9db-47f8-93f6-40ab2da735d0",
      "claimId": "claim:4a2698ee-a454-4596-bdc9-acc4518f8f82",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-5d7a6b142c0fa257859e956fb06390f46da8ab288257ffebd2bef74da17d6893"
      },
      "text": "All L sparsification steps succeed with probability at least 1 − Lη' = 1 − η (union bound over the L product-region steps).",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-8d129a91aafe22d4ee860538a0c107523398f9594ec3d3f7dbe171b0682ff4e8",
      "kind": "probability",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-5d7a6b142c0fa257859e956fb06390f46da8ab288257ffebd2bef74da17d6893"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:f01b4ce2-0d62-4065-9f86-09cacfcfc1ae",
      "claimId": "claim:1ec5e44e-1e9a-4992-8e6b-7d3917eca5e8",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-f68a44ae40f37cbad437f5a37ab1311cf531dc64747d0a18f78a6064ea638bdf"
      },
      "text": "Each sparsification call retains at most m = O(W log(2W)/δ² log(1/η')) rows; hence M = O(W L² log(2W)/ε² · log(L/η)).",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-69483c48f6bc20c5cc0c4db96b12fc6fb45ef30996707a54ab5c8b496efd0a83",
      "kind": "space",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-f68a44ae40f37cbad437f5a37ab1311cf531dc64747d0a18f78a6064ea638bdf"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:6bf42963-6ca5-49c8-95f4-a9dfc0a23fef",
      "claimId": "claim:d85dbfc6-a912-4392-81d5-7db369db9566",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-e2a81639348426e4a714735a25f925c5d03f02a993b580884968e348d449a6b7"
      },
      "text": "Every binary product region has at most (q+M)² candidate rows (children are leaves with ≤ q rows or internal with ≤ M rows).",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-50ccc323be4e783bd5df948ee6b95b02bd2a1e16990c0d5fb6b49a2b70b953ea",
      "kind": "resource",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-e2a81639348426e4a714735a25f925c5d03f02a993b580884968e348d449a6b7"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:f85ad484-ade0-4019-ae35-f5791a9cf97a",
      "claimId": "claim:8d9ab7e9-1910-4ae9-9b97-f1be1fb68a1e",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-3e2834834ad61f729c391327fc8151007b7bd1239b765b459b0b43012087e57f"
      },
      "text": "The product-stage feature matrix has O(W) columns, so the Lewis weights of one region cost Õ((q+M)²W + W^ω) arithmetic operations.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-be9cdd4827556378317254a335a5acad03bd0e0ecbee77cf26dddba0adba7f1e",
      "kind": "time",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-3e2834834ad61f729c391327fc8151007b7bd1239b765b459b0b43012087e57f"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:513bad9f-dc6f-463d-94aa-c82142ee3cab",
      "claimId": "claim:7388f216-468d-4992-842b-2317bdb18b04",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-d7542d80255ee961e7e5c0b310cdd9e197eb4ce56eea5f38aca5d54e18eccc5f"
      },
      "text": "Evaluating the exact leaf tables of both circuits costs O(q|C|); applying all subsequent gates and wires to surviving rows only costs O(M|C|).",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-4316c462b64eba228981730633909ceac83347e5aa71edf7811a17c1fffba569",
      "kind": "time",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "main.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-d7542d80255ee961e7e5c0b310cdd9e197eb4ce56eea5f38aca5d54e18eccc5f"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:4345a6f6-30ca-4ebd-9ca2-485f4c001072",
      "claimId": "claim:4e08af5f-a7c2-4887-bce4-81540301481c",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:323bbbaf-d7f0-4120-930c-9331b3c1bc9f",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "main.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-2f72d72c53f38762ce53e16a850fd421dd45bc3989be43cee8cb6e09c625b711"
      },
      "text": "Total arithmetic running time Õ((q+M)|C| + L[W(q+M)² + W^ω]).",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-cdd983d5ec8059bd135e0845a7ba4cae1a6958e9f4aeb7eccaed1575e10ccfc9",
      "kind": "time",
      "evidence": [
